      "bio_summary": {
        "value": "Growing up in rural Ohio, I learned the true meaning of hard work, responsibility, and the importance of community. These values were instilled in me by my family and the close-knit community that surrounded us. It’s this upbringing that has shaped my principles and guided me throughout my life. ‍ I ran for Congress because I saw the challenges plaguing our country, challenges that hit close to home. Out of control spending, skyrocketing cost of living, parents worried about what their kids were seeing both in and out of the classroom, and many Americans feeling left behind - these are issues that I couldn’t ignore.",
